WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.095
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:08.607
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.907 --> 00:00:14.706
Unit twelve: Leaders We Admire. In this unit, you will describe what makes a good leader.

4
00:00:15.717 --> 00:00:16.532
Leader.

5
00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:19.824
Leader means a person who guides and helps a group.

6
00:00:20.124 --> 00:00:21.903
A good leader listens to people.

7
00:00:22.603 --> 00:00:25.081
Your turn. Say: Leader.

8
00:00:27.781 --> 00:00:28.666
Leader.

9
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:30.500
Admire.

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.070
Admire means to like and respect someone very much.

11
00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.975
I admire my grandfather.

12
00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:39.409
Your turn. Say: Admire.

13
00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:42.994
Admire.

14
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:44.729
Brave.

15
00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:48.009
Brave means not afraid to do difficult things.

16
00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:50.181
Firefighters are very brave.

17
00:00:50.881 --> 00:00:53.661
Your turn. Say: Brave.

18
00:00:56.361 --> 00:00:57.072
Brave.

19
00:00:58.083 --> 00:00:58.957
Honest.

20
00:00:59.657 --> 00:01:02.190
Honest means always telling the truth.

21
00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.875
Leaders should be honest.

22
00:01:04.575 --> 00:01:06.658
Your turn. Say: Honest.

23
00:01:09.358 --> 00:01:10.208
Honest.

24
00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:11.916
Fair.

25
00:01:12.616 --> 00:01:15.184
Fair means treating everyone in the same right way.

26
00:01:15.484 --> 00:01:18.006
Our class monitor is fair to everyone.

27
00:01:18.706 --> 00:01:21.115
Your turn. Say: Fair.

28
00:01:23.815 --> 00:01:24.665
Fair.

29
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.744
Inspire.

30
00:01:27.444 --> 00:01:30.221
Inspire means to make someone want to do something good.

31
00:01:30.521 --> 00:01:32.440
My teacher inspires me to read.

32
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.862
Your turn. Say: Inspire.

33
00:01:38.562 --> 00:01:39.551
Inspire.

34
00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:41.261
Help.

35
00:01:41.961 --> 00:01:44.332
Help means to make things easier for someone.

36
00:01:44.632 --> 00:01:46.759
Good leaders help their communities.

37
00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:50.158
Your turn. Say: Help.

38
00:01:52.858 --> 00:01:53.673
Help.

39
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:55.615
Change.

40
00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.744
Change means something that becomes different.

41
00:01:59.044 --> 00:02:01.322
She brought positive change to our village.

42
00:02:02.022 --> 00:02:04.686
Your turn. Say: Change.

43
00:02:07.386 --> 00:02:08.225
Change.

44
00:02:09.217 --> 00:02:11.112
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:11.412 --> 00:02:13.678
Sreypich, who is a leader you admire?

46
00:02:14.983 --> 00:02:16.913
I admire our school principal.

47
00:02:18.217 --> 00:02:19.195
Why?

48
00:02:20.483 --> 00:02:23.702
She is fair and honest, and she inspires the students.

49
00:02:25.017 --> 00:02:26.505
What should a good leader be like?

50
00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:30.641
A leader should be brave and should be kind to everyone.

51
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.401
Grammar focus: Should plus be plus adjective.

52
00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.631
A leader should be honest and fair.

53
00:02:37.931 --> 00:02:42.101
After 'should', use 'be' + an adjective to describe how someone ought to act.

54
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:45.873
Now read and listen. A Leader I Admire.

55
00:02:46.173 --> 00:02:48.800
The leader I admire most is my village chief.

56
00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:52.362
He is honest and fair to every family.

57
00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.684
He was brave when there was a big flood.

58
00:02:56.983 --> 00:02:59.320
He inspires young people to help the village.

59
00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:03.951
I think every leader should be kind and should listen to people.

60
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.914
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:08.214 --> 00:03:10.005
A leader should blank honest.

62
00:03:10.305 --> 00:03:13.308
A, be. B, is. C, being.

63
00:03:17.317 --> 00:03:19.305
The answer is A: be.

64
00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:23.559
To like and respect someone very much is to blank.

65
00:03:23.859 --> 00:03:27.675
A, admire. B, inspire. C, change.

66
00:03:31.683 --> 00:03:33.578
The answer is A: admire.

67
00:03:35.083 --> 00:03:37.687
Treating everyone in the same right way is blank.

68
00:03:37.987 --> 00:03:41.443
A, fair. B, brave. C, famous.

69
00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.438
The answer is A: fair.

70
00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:53.010
Now it's your turn to speak. Who is a leader you admire? Why?

71
00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:04.120
I admire my teacher because she is honest and fair. I think a leader should be brave and should help people.

72
00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.094
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:11.686
Great work today! You learned eight new words and should plus be plus adjective.

74
00:04:11.986 --> 00:04:16.728
Today's value is leadership. Lead fairly, listen to others and set a good example.

75
00:04:17.028 --> 00:04:19.750
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.563
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

